We start with a menu that maps symbols to prices: menu = { coffee: 1299, mug: 850, beans: 999 }
we take the names and sort them: names = menu.keys.sort

Then we print every name and its price.

names.each { |name| puts "#{name}: #{menu[name]}" }

and we find the cheapest price: cheapest = menu.values.min
then we print it: puts !-1
and add one cent: puts !-1 + 1
